#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133401 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "216b16aa-d279-519e-a749-b9fd5517a6db" :question/math-academy-id "e-11507" :question/problem "Find the missing limits in the repeated integral below\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \nf(x,y,z) \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region defined as\n\n$$\nR=\\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: -3 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\: x \\leq z \\leq 2x+2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq z+xz \\right\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Retain the defining inequalities of $R$ exactly. Ordered $z$ bounds require $x\\le2x+2$, so $x\\ge-2$. A nonempty $y$ fiber requires $(1+x)z\\ge0$. For $-2\\le x\\le-1$, both $1+x$ and every allowed $z$ are nonpositive. For $-1\\le x\\le0$, keep only $z\\ge0$. For $0\\le x\\le3$, the printed lower bound $z=x$ is already nonnegative. Therefore\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R f\\,dV={}&\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\int_x^{2x+2}\\int_0^{z+xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\\\\&+\\int_{-1}^{0}\\int_0^{2x+2}\\int_0^{z+xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\\\\&+\\int_0^{3}\\int_x^{2x+2}\\int_0^{z+xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThese three integrals cover the actual region with ordered bounds; boundary overlap has measure zero. For $f=1$, their volumes are $5/24$, $1/2$, and $903/8$, totaling $1363/12$. The source solution used $x\\in[-3,3]$ and $z\\in[x,2x+2]$ throughout, including reversed or empty fibers; its formal signed integral gives $111$ and does not integrate over $R$."}]}
